---
import SidebarLayout from "../../layouts/SideBarLayout.astro";
---

<SidebarLayout title="Liquiprism (2024)">
    <h1>Liquiprism (2024)</h1>
    <p>
        The Liquiprism web app is inspired by the landmark paper that introduced
        the Liquiprism [1]: a 3D cube containing cellular automata on each face.
        These faces are sonified through the cellular activity in order to
        generate polyphonic music.
    </p>
    <p>
        To develop this application, I designed the Liquiprism's architecture,
        consisting of its logic, visualisation, and sonification, using
        JavaScript and TypeScript. I implemented the application with the
        Astro.js framework and deployed it with Vercel.
    </p>
    <p>
        The website is available at <a
            href="https://liquiprism.vercel.app"
            target="_blank">liquiprism.vercel.app</a
        >. And you can find the code <a
            href="https://github.com/theofuhrmann/liquiprism_app"
            target="_blank">here</a
        >.
    </p>
    <img
        src="/images/Liquiprism_2.png"
        alt="Liquiprism"
        style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; width: 600px; align-self: center;"
    />
    <p>
        [1] Dorin, Alan. "LiquiPrism: Generating polyrhythms with cellular
        automata." <i
            >Proceedings of the 2002 International Conference on
            AuditoryDisplay, Kyoto, Japan, July 2.</i
        > Vol. 5. 2002.
    </p>
</SidebarLayout>
